//     call site by hand.
//   - =~ with /g in list context (/^([a-z]*):(.*)/g) — Perl returns every captured group across all 
//     matches; JS .match() with /g returns only full-match strings, not captures. Verify this call 
//     site by hand.
//   - =~ with /g in list context (/^Category: (.*)/) — Perl returns every captured group across all 
//     matches; JS .match() with /g returns only full-match strings, not captures. Verify this call 
//     site by hand.
//   - =~ with /g in list context (/^(description|title)\:(.*)/g) — Perl returns every captured 
//     group across all matches; JS .match() with /g returns only full-match strings, not captures. 
//     Verify this call site by hand.
//   - =~ with /g in list context (/^https\:\/\/(e.hentai\.org\/g\/[0-9]*\/[0-z]*)\/*.*/gi) — Perl 
//     returns every captured group across all matches; JS .match() with /g returns only full-match 
//     strings, not captures. Verify this call site by hand.
//   - =~ with /g in list context (/^Language: ([a-z]*)/i) — Perl returns every captured group 
//     across all matches; JS .match() with /g returns only full-match strings, not captures. Verify 
//     this call site by hand.
//   - =~ with /g in list context (/^Tags:/) — Perl returns every captured group across all matches; 
//     JS .match() with /g returns only full-match strings, not captures. Verify this call site by 
//     hand.
//   - external Perl module reference has no JS equivalent: Time::Piece
//   - this plugin declares 3 custom parameters, but the host currently passes only one generic 
//     `arg` value per call — only `replace_title` was mapped to it; the rest were also bound to 
